## Description

This detection identifies the execution of **PowerShell commands using the `-EncodedCommand` parameter** through **Microsoft Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation)**.

PowerShell supports Base64-encoded command execution using the `-EncodedCommand` argument. While this feature is legitimate and commonly used for automation, threat actors frequently abuse it to obfuscate malicious scripts, bypass security controls, and evade detection.

Monitoring encoded PowerShell execution provides defenders with high-fidelity visibility into suspicious PowerShell activity.

