# Analyst Notes

Encoded PowerShell is one of the most common techniques observed in phishing campaigns, malware loaders, ransomware, and post-exploitation frameworks because it hides the original command from casual inspection.

While legitimate administrative tools occasionally use encoded commands, defenders should treat every occurrence as potentially suspicious until the encoded payload has been decoded and verified.

This detection provides high-value visibility into obfuscated PowerShell execution and forms an essential component of endpoint detection strategies for Windows environments.
